# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Receipts — environment
#
# The app degrades honestly rather than failing: with no keys at all it runs in
# DEMO_MODE + FIXTURE_MODE and is fully clickable. Each key you add switches one
# layer from stub to live. Nothing here is ever exposed to the browser.
#
# ⚠ PLACEHOLDERS ONLY. No real host, index, slug, document id or key belongs in
# this file — it is committed, and anything in it is permanent in history once
# the repo is public. Real values go in an untracked .env locally and in the
# host's secret store in production.
#
# This file is kept in sync with config.ts by a test (config.env.test.ts): a var
# added to the code without a line here, or a line here the code never reads,
# fails the suite. A documented knob that does nothing is worse than an
# undocumented one — someone sets it and believes it took effect.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Anthropic — classification, explanation, and the tool-use loop ────────────
# Without this, DEMO_MODE turns on and interpret/explain use deterministic stubs.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Ceiling for one streamed turn. NOT a spend target — billing is on tokens
# generated, so headroom is free and truncation is not. Adaptive thinking counts
# against this. Sonnet 5 caps at 128k.
ANTHROPIC_MAX_TOKENS=64000

# ── Models — deliberately NOT single-vendor ──────────────────────────────────
# Fulfillment stays on OpenAI to match the model that scored the whole corpus.
# Consolidating these to one vendor is a known tempting mistake, not a cleanup.
#
# classify is PROVISIONAL: parity is owed against the GPT-4.1 corpus labels.
# Overridable here so the 12-row check can swap it without a code change.
CLASSIFY_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5
FULFILL_MODEL=gpt-5.4-mini
EXPLAIN_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5

# ── OpenAI — embeds the user's promise, and runs relevance + fulfillment ──────
# EMBEDDING_* must match the batch pipeline exactly. Changing either breaks
# parity with the stored vectors — the query lands in a different space and
# match quality degrades silently, with no error.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
EMBEDDING_MODEL=text-embedding-3-small
EMBEDDING_DIMENSIONS=1024

# ── Pinecone — the senator's already-embedded bills/actions ──────────────────
PINECONE_API_KEY=
# Index host, no trailing slash. PLACEHOLDER — substitute your own.
PINECONE_HOST=https://your-index.svc.your-region.pinecone.io
PINECONE_INDEX=your-index
# Namespace template. {politician_id} is substituted per query. Bills/actions
# live in {politician_id}_bills; promise vectors (used only by the deferred
# provenance lookup) live in _statements.
PINECONE_NAMESPACE_TEMPLATE={politician_id}_bills
# Batch runs filter bill vectors by embedding_version == run_id. A live query
# has no run to scope to. Leave BLANK to search all versions.
#
# A stale pin returns zero vectors from a full namespace, which would otherwise
# render as "no relevant bills" — a finding produced by a config typo. When this
# is set and the query returns nothing, PineconeActionStore fails loudly instead.
PINECONE_EMBEDDING_VERSION=

# ── Retrieval ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
RETRIEVAL_TOP_K=10
# NOTE: the similarity floors (STRONG 0.575 / WEAK 0.50) are NOT env-tunable.
# They are ports of WF7a's thresholds and live in scoring/config.ts, because
# changing them makes Receipts disagree with the senator profile. Editing them
# is a port-reconciliation task, logged in RECONCILIATION — not a deploy knob.

# ── Feature flags ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Lets a user assert "he promised this", upgrading the wording to KEPT/BROKE.
# Ships OFF pending copy review: printing "BROKE" against a commitment we have
# no evidence was made is the one output with real downside.
ENABLE_CAMPAIGN_PROMISE_OVERRIDE=false

# ── Mode overrides (normally inferred from which keys are present) ───────────
# FIXTURE_MODE=true  -> canned matches, no OpenAI/Pinecone calls
# DEMO_MODE=true     -> deterministic interpret/explain, no Anthropic calls
FIXTURE_MODE=
DEMO_MODE=

# ── Supabase / Postgres — query + session persistence ────────────────────────
# MUST connect as the `receipts_app` role. Never `postgres`, never a
# service_role key: the corpus firewall is built out of roles, and
# `receipts_trust` being locked out of the app schema only means anything if the
# app connects as the role that is actually walled.
#
# Prefer the TRANSACTION-MODE POOLER (port 6543) over a direct 5432 connection —
# a persistent server should not hold a real Postgres backend open.
#
#   postgresql://receipts_app.<project-ref>:<password>@<region>.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres
#
# Blank -> NullQueryStore: the app boots and answers queries, but persists
# nothing and share links resolve to nothing.
DATABASE_URL=

# ── Coverage disclosure ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Congresses whose legislation has been collected and embedded, comma-separated.
#
# DISCLOSURE, not a filter — retrieval already searches only what exists in the
# namespace. This is so the tool can SAY what it searched.
#
# Without it, "we found no bills or votes on this" reads as "the senator has no
# record on this", and for anything outside the window that is false. Schumer
# passed the Inflation Reduction Act in the 117th; the corpus starts at the
# 118th, so his defining drug-pricing legislation would be reported as an
# absence of action.
#
# Blank means the window is UNKNOWN, and the tool says so rather than implying
# full coverage.
COVERAGE_CONGRESSES=118,119

# ── CORS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Comma-separated origins allowed to call this API. BLANK = allow any, which is
# fine locally and wrong in production: every request spends money at three
# vendors, so an open policy is an open invoice. Set this to the deployed
# frontend origin, e.g. https://receipts.vercel.app
CORS_ORIGIN=

# ── Google Sheets document ids (unused today) ────────────────────────────────
# data/sheets.ts is imported nowhere; the Supabase mirror supersedes it. These
# stay env-driven with no defaults so real document ids can never return to the
# committed tree — a Sheets doc id is an access identifier, not a name.
SHEETS_DOC_CORPUS=
SHEETS_DOC_ALIGNMENT=
SHEETS_DOC_IMPACT=
SHEETS_DOC_TAXONOMY=

# ── Ports ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# API_PORT wins over PORT. The indirection matters in dev, where the API and
# Vite run side by side under one environment and hosts inject PORT for whatever
# they think the single service is. PORT alone is correct in production.
API_PORT=
PORT=8787
